## Knowledge — substrate invariants

### Invariant A — Adapter purity

`KnowledgeSourceAdapter.listDocuments` returns plain `RawKnowledgeDocument` items only.
Adapters must **not**: write DB rows, call embedding functions, choose chunking strategy, influence ranking.
Only `pipeline-commit.ts` may write `knowledge_document` or `knowledge_chunk`.

### Invariant B — Retrieval is source-blind

Retrieval and reranking must not branch on `knowledge_source.kind`. Do not join source metadata for ranking heuristics. Allowed inputs: tenant id, query, optional explicit document allowlists.

### Invariant C — Embedding runs outside Route Handlers

Never call `embedKnowledgeBatch` inline in a Route Handler. Embedding runs in background jobs (cron + queue). Embedding in Route Handlers for single queries (truth search, operator tool) is acceptable only when the query is user-initiated and the latency budget is known.

### Invariant D — Tenant isolation

All queries include `WHERE organization_id = $orgId`. RLS policies are defense-in-depth — app-level filters are still mandatory.

